## 7. Authentication Flow

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant U as User
    participant F as Frontend
    participant S as Supabase Auth
    participant B as Backend API

    U->>F: Enter email & password
    F->>S: supabase.auth.signUp() / signInWithPassword()
    S-->>F: JWT access_token + refresh_token
    F->>F: Store session (Supabase handles)

    Note over F,B: Subsequent API calls
    F->>B: GET /api/trips (Authorization: Bearer <JWT>)
    B->>S: Verify JWT via Supabase public key
    S-->>B: Decoded user { id, email, role }
    B->>B: Fetch user's trips from DB
    B-->>F: JSON response

    Note over F,S: Token refresh (automatic)
    F->>S: supabase.auth.refreshSession()
    S-->>F: New JWT
```

### Authentication Strategy Details

- **Supabase Auth** handles signup, login, password reset, email verification
- **JWT** with 1-hour expiry; auto-refresh handled by `@supabase/supabase-js`
- **Backend middleware** decodes JWT using Supabase public key — zero password storage on our end
- **Row Level Security (RLS)** in Supabase as a defense-in-depth layer
- **Rate limiting** via Redis: 100 requests/min per IP for auth endpoints

